    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "yHlal",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3100,
      "name": "836 terminal size notes",
      "width": 4560,
      "height": 300,
      "content": "836 · Terminal size (spec: docs/features/836-web-remote-control.md, Phase 2 › Terminal size, on nightly-remote). Jason's direction, 2026-10-19: while another device controls a terminal, the desktop covers it the way the two-window case covers a duplicate chat (ui/duplicate_subject_overlay.rs): an 85% bg scrim and a centered card, cmp/ControlledCard. Take back is the only way back, by its button or Enter, so desktop keystrokes never land in a terminal a browser is using, and the desktop never draws a grid sized for another device. A browser opens what the sidebar holds, a tab or a mission, as a unit, taking every terminal in it; a chat has no sidebar row of its own, so it is never taken apart from its tab. One card therefore covers the whole tab or mission below its tab bar, and Take back returns each terminal to its own pane. Frames: a browser has control; the browser has left; a browser opened a split tab; light theme with Chinese strings; and the existing two-window overlay for comparison. The browser's own side, the scaled view with Take control, is the web panel's."
    }
